                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c752411a-eecd-3426-b040-7d73d9be25d3",
                                        "entry_id": "a6629725-821b-3693-8947-4ea83981c79c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to charity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb82aa6a-6a0a-35eb-b889-f8de75eb8439",
                                        "entry_id": "a6629725-821b-3693-8947-4ea83981c79c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Kind, generous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbccdf60-f1af-4d51-a9f8-1c5f91c3eb40",
                                                "sense_id": "bb82aa6a-6a0a-35eb-b889-f8de75eb8439",
                                                "text": "St. Martin [of Tours] looks round, first, deliberately;—becomes aware of a tatterdemalion and thirsty-looking soul of a beggar at his chair side, who has managed to get his cup filled somehow, also—by a charitable lacquey. St. Martin turns his back on the Empress, and hobnobs with him!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf703d98-4bcc-4455-b2d2-b047204f7f0e",
                                                "sense_id": "bb82aa6a-6a0a-35eb-b889-f8de75eb8439",
                                                "text": "Pakistan can sometimes be a cruel environment, its residents caught between the dual pressures of poverty and violence. Yet it is also a place of great kindness, with a strong culture of charitable giving."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5daf6008-3b5e-3dda-9b94-1d2aff6529a1",
                                        "entry_id": "a6629725-821b-3693-8947-4ea83981c79c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a purpose or character of a charity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1726c595-09a9-493c-b8a6-00fbc84b0e4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "b2cf3fbf-8722-3235-8c0c-194197785efe",
                        "source_sense_id": "88a4f8fd-52aa-33e3-9564-ab22b2eec1ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "lenient",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lenient",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "836043da-4461-3f70-8217-ac56b1a1cb54",
                                        "entry_id": "fd77c0e9-cb83-3417-8781-1f4f100de24f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lax; not strict; tolerant of dissent or deviation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c3f47f3-1442-4df0-8250-93873a08fa79",
                                                "sense_id": "836043da-4461-3f70-8217-ac56b1a1cb54",
                                                "text": "The standard is fairly lenient, so use your discretion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1731d41-d014-49b1-a84a-b5ed617c2df5",
                                                "sense_id": "836043da-4461-3f70-8217-ac56b1a1cb54",
                                                "text": "But in other points, as well as this, I was growing very lenient to my master; I was forgetting all his faults, for which I had once kept a sharp look-out. It had formerly been my endeavour to study all sides of his character; to take the bad with the good; and from the just weighing of both, to form an equitable judgment. Now I saw no bad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lenient",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bffc23e-241e-3609-9137-58d0cb6de6a5",
                                        "entry_id": "e4902179-30f0-3223-9a71-e7098cf94070",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lenitive; an emollient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "600a7bff-d699-4b83-8075-7910b369e229",
                        "source_entry_id": "b2cf3fbf-8722-3235-8c0c-194197785efe",
                        "source_sense_id": "88a4f8fd-52aa-33e3-9564-ab22b2eec1ee",
                        "target_lang_word": "merciful",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "merciful",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "976de63a-574b-3958-bf28-456d0e3d6a03",
                                        "entry_id": "88b292bd-1cf9-3781-bed5-39f8768ebb6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing mercy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9305944-2414-4505-88f6-ad74bd6d93cd",
                                                "sense_id": "976de63a-574b-3958-bf28-456d0e3d6a03",
                                                "text": "`Listen, Holly. Thou art a good and honest man, and I fain would spare thee; but, oh! it is so hard for woman to be merciful.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "213c4b27-4aa7-42d8-a1b6-bb8fcc1ad9a5",
                                                "sense_id": "976de63a-574b-3958-bf28-456d0e3d6a03",
                                                "text": "The murderer, he recalled, had been tried and sentenced to imprisonment for life, but was pardoned by a merciful governor after serving a year of his sentence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
